@aojea Thanks for the feedback!

**Re: Shutdown safety:** Yes, immediate cancellation is intended here. Since the etcd connection is usually already dying when stopCh closes, "graceful" waiting is exactly what triggers the retry loop/leak. Immediate cancellation stops that safely.

**Re: Refactor:** That makes sense. I initially chose the minimal patch to limit the blast radius, but I agree that aligning with the pattern in 7eb7894 would be cleaner. I will take a look at refactoring the controller to be fully context-aware and, if it works out cleanly, I'll update the PR.

