comments.comment_body_raw:
@liggitt what you described is correct, it is the current behavior for regular extended resource. the formula is given in https://github.com/kubernetes/enhancements/tree/master/keps/sig-node/753-sidecar-containers#resources-calculation-for-scheduling-and-pod-admission

however, for DRA extended resources, we use device requests to allocate the devices at the scheduling time, and map the device requests to container's resource requests, also at the scheduling time. so we can have non sidecar init container device request: example.com:3 and map that device request to the non sidecar init container that requests for example.com: 1. The inverse is tricky to do. that is, we have three device requests, each for a container request for example.com: 1, it's not easy to map that three device requests to one init container that requests for example.com: 3

in short, the current PR's implementation is an improvement over the one device request per container per extended resource, but it is not the optimial formula as given https://github.com/kubernetes/enhancements/tree/master/keps/sig-node/753-sidecar-containers#resources-calculation-for-scheduling-and-pod-admission, which requries splitting a bigger device request into smaller ones for containers that request for smaller ones, and also combine smaller device requests into bigger ones for contaienrs that request for bigger ones.

