I added a temporary commit [temp-isolation-level](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/134768/commits/3d105fb96c61fd642b2e9992b71668710e0cfabc) to discuss about the implementation of the isolation level to handle the CPU quota accordingly. Followed your suggestion https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/134768#pullrequestreview-3439861162, and defined three isolation levels:
```
const (
	// ResourceIsolationHost implies the resource is shared with other containers on the host.
	ResourceIsolationHost ResourceIsolationLevel = iota
	// ResourceIsolationPod implies the resource is isolated from other pods but shared within the pod.
	ResourceIsolationPod
	// ResourceIsolationContainer implies the resource is exclusive to the container.
	ResourceIsolationContainer
)
```

The new function would look like this (after `PodLevelResourceManagers` becomes GA, only the code inside the feature gate check would be needed):
```
func (cm *containerManagerImpl) ContainerHasExclusiveCPUs(pod *v1.Pod, container *v1.Container) bool {
	if utilfeature.DefaultFeatureGate.Enabled(kubefeatures.PodLevelResourceManagers) {
		if cm.cpuManager.GetResourceIsolationLevel(pod, container) != cmqos.ResourceIsolationContainer {
